{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790963053,"nonce":"c2y4rjjukyY68XNkBk5Gwwr18a0=","message":"Backends: caribou-gpu, rayzor-gpu and hlwgpu wrap the same xgpu core (../xgpu) and expose the same generated `gpu` API, so the renderer is written once against `gpu.*` and the runtime is picked by compile flag, with #if only around what differs:\n- async: hlwgpu returns ash.Future\u003cT\u003e; check the other adapters' equivalent;\n- windows and surfaces: Caribou has the cb_window plugin (caribou/plugins/cb_window), Rayzor has examples/gpu-window, Ash/HashLink has no public window library (hlwgpu's crates/hlwindow is a test helper, and xgpu's README lists the Ash adapter as being realigned);\n- the Blinc side: ashui's Blinc ABI is HashLink-only today, so on Caribou and Rayzor the layout tree needs their own bindings before anything draws there.\n\nFirst milestone that needs no window: render the laid-out tree to an offscreen texture on Ash, read it back and check pixels, which is the spec's phase 2 validation.","files":null}]}